To Store and retrieve files using AWS S3
Task
1. Open Amazon S3 from the AWS Console.
2. Create a new S3 bucket with default settings.
3. Upload files such as images and text documents.
4. Configure public access permissions for uploaded files.
5. Access and verify the uploaded files using S3 URLs



2. Open Amazon S3

In top search bar type:

S3
Open
Amazon Simple Storage Service
3. Create S3 Bucket
Open Buckets Section
Left sidebar → Buckets

Click:

Create bucket
Configure Bucket
Bucket Name

Enter unique bucket name.

Example:

sahil-demo-bucket-123
AWS Region

Select nearest region.

Example:

Asia Pacific (Mumbai) ap-south-1
Keep Default Settings

Do NOT change anything else.

Create Bucket

Scroll down and click:

Create bucket

Bucket created successfully.

4. Open the Bucket

Click on your bucket name:

sahil-demo-bucket-123
5. Upload Files
Upload Images/Text Files

Click:

Upload

Click:

Add files
Select:
image files
text files
from your computer
Upload

Click:

Upload

Files uploaded successfully.

6. Configure Public Access

By default files are private.

We now make files publicly accessible.

Disable Block Public Access
Open uploaded file

Click:

Permissions

Scroll to:

Block public access

Click:

Edit

Untick:

Block all public access
Tick acknowledgment checkbox

Click:

Save changes
7. Make File Public
Open Object Permissions
Open uploaded file

Go to:

Permissions
Edit Object Access

Scroll to:

Object Ownership / Access Control List (ACL)

Click:

Edit
Grant Public Read Access

Under:

Everyone (public access)

Tick:

Read
Save changes

Public access enabled.

8. Access File Using S3 URL
Copy Object URL
Open uploaded file
Scroll down

Find:

Object URL

Example:

https://sahil-demo-bucket-123.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/sample.txt
9. Verify Uploaded File
Copy Object URL
Open new browser tab
Paste URL
